// Geolocation enrichment for public failed logons.
// Run this from Microsoft Sentinel, Logs. Pick the law-home-soc-lab workspace.
// Three approaches are below. Use Approach A unless you are practising watchlists.
// None of these queries ship location data. They return rows only from your SecurityEvent table.
// IP geolocation is approximate. Do not treat a city result as a street address.
// TimeGenerated is UTC.

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Approach A. Built in lookup, geo_info_from_ip_address()
// Documented for Microsoft Sentinel and Azure Monitor.
// It uses the GeoLite2 city data that the KQL function already includes.
// You do not upload a database and you do not pay a third party.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1d)
| where EventID == 4625
| where LogonType in (3, 10)
| where isnotempty(IpAddress) and IpAddress != "-"
| where ipv4_is_private(IpAddress) == false
| extend Geo = geo_info_from_ip_address(IpAddress)
| extend Country = tostring(Geo.country)
| extend State = tostring(Geo.state)
| extend City = tostring(Geo.city)
| extend Latitude = toreal(Geo.latitude)
| extend Longitude = toreal(Geo.longitude)
| summarize FailedLogons = count(), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated)
    by IpAddress, Country, State, City, Latitude, Longitude, Computer
| order by FailedLogons desc

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Approach B. Sentinel watchlist, exact IP match.
// Create the watchlist yourself. Steps are in docs/lab-guide.md.
// Alias: GeoIP
// CSV header, saved only on your machine, not in git:
// SearchKey,Country,City,Latitude,Longitude
// SearchKey is one public IP per row, copied from your own query results.
// Do not commit that CSV. .gitignore already ignores *.csv.
// Uncomment this block and comment out Approach A when the watchlist exists.
// An empty Country column means that IP is not on the watchlist yet.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// let Geo = _GetWatchlist("GeoIP")
// | project SearchKey, Country, City, Latitude = toreal(Latitude), Longitude = toreal(Longitude);
// SecurityEvent
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(1d)
// | where EventID == 4625
// | where LogonType in (3, 10)
// | where isnotempty(IpAddress) and IpAddress != "-"
// | where ipv4_is_private(IpAddress) == false
// | join kind=leftouter (Geo) on $left.IpAddress == $right.SearchKey
// | project TimeGenerated, Computer, Account, IpAddress, Country, City, Latitude, Longitude

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Approach C. ipv4_lookup for CIDR ranges.
// The plugin is documented for Azure Data Explorer and Microsoft Fabric.
// Sentinel Logs may accept it. If you get a syntax error, stay with Approach A or B.
// Replace the documentation range below with CIDR rows you looked up yourself.
// 203.0.113.0/24 is TEST-NET-3 from RFC 5737. It is not a location feed and it will not match real scanners.
// Do not point external_data at a downloaded GeoIP file in this lab.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// let Ranges = datatable(network:string, Note:string)
// [
//     "203.0.113.0/24", "TEST-NET-3 documentation range. Replace this row with ranges you looked up."
// ];
// SecurityEvent
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(1d)
// | where EventID == 4625
// | where isnotempty(IpAddress) and IpAddress != "-"
// | evaluate ipv4_lookup(Ranges, IpAddress, network, return_unmatched = true)
// | project TimeGenerated, Computer, Account, IpAddress, network, Note
